<!--
  Quick Settings tile badge.

  The intrinsic size is deliberately 40dp instead of the 24dp the Android docs
  suggest for tile icons. Measured on HyperOS (Android 15): a tile icon is
  drawn at its own intrinsic size inside the ~48-55dp round tile background
  and is never scaled up, so 24dp drawables (all system tiles) cover only
  ~40% of the circle while a third-party tile shipping a ~44dp drawable
  covers ~85%. A 24dp badge is therefore always in the smallest tier.
  Keeping viewport at 24 units and raising only width/height scales the same
  artwork up by 40/24. Platforms that force the icon into a fixed 20-24dp
  frame (AOSP QSIconViewImpl measures its ImageView at qs_icon_size with
  FIT_CENTER) scale it back down again, so this stays safe there.

  The traced outline is fitted to 23.4 x 18.2 units of the 24 unit viewport:
  it is already flush horizontally (only 0.2 unit of breathing room per side),
  while the remaining vertical blank is inherent to the mascot's wide, flat
  aspect ratio (432x333 in ic_launcher_mascot.png).
-->
